{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded","id":1510845,"title":"Technocracy reloaded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-05T18:25:17-07:00","id":1510845,"title":"Technocracy reloaded","content":"Is it worth it? <br /> <br /> Or to be more precise how is it different than guide to technocracy aside from moving the setting by a couple of decades <br /> In general I am deeply skeptical about rewrites, so is it worth it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T18:33:59-07:00","id":1510846,"title":"","content":"It adjusts the Technocracy to be even less two-dimensional villains than Guide to the Technocracy had them; and that's saying a lot. For instance, TR explains that Technocrats <i>don't </i>disbelieve in Magick; they just see Magick as a dangerous and unpredictable cousin to their own Enlightened Science. There are several other points in the book that recast the Union in a less stereotype-driven light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T19:14:57-07:00","id":1510848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded?p=1510846#post1510846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It adjusts the Technocracy to be even less two-dimensional villains than Guide to the Technocracy had them; and that's saying a lot. For instance, TR explains that Technocrats <i>don't </i>disbelieve in Magick; they just see Magick as a dangerous and unpredictable cousin to their own Enlightened Science. There are several other points in the book that recast the Union in a less stereotype-driven light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally. I always thought the idea of making technocrats be THAT ignorant was insanity lol. It was so crazy that I had difficulty convincing people that it worked that way. <br /> <br /> For instance, I always pictured a nwo agent saying &quot; OK I get it fairies are real you stupid blood witch, but if they are real then man-eating dragons are real too. Freedom of thought is a good theory, but not when the universe cares only about what you believe is true, rather than what you wish were true, so don't you dare convince people otherwise or billions will die&quot;<br /> <br /> I assume it works like the sorcerers crusade where upon reaching a certain rank, you are told that they are the same, but until then you see them as distinct?<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you mind telling me about the other points? Uhm just a sentence each would be more than enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T21:55:08-07:00","id":1510859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded?p=1510846#post1510846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It adjusts the Technocracy to be even less two-dimensional villains than Guide to the Technocracy had them; and that's saying a lot. For instance, TR explains that Technocrats <i>don't </i>disbelieve in Magick; they just see Magick as a dangerous and unpredictable cousin to their own Enlightened Science. There are several other points in the book that recast the Union in a less stereotype-driven light.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> if I remember correctly, the book states that technocracts are in a 1984 doublethink state on that matter. Both accepting and denying magic at the the same time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T22:22:34-07:00","id":1510860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded?p=1510848#post1510848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, I always pictured a nwo agent saying &quot; OK I get it fairies are real you stupid blood witch, but if they are real then man-eating dragons are real too. Freedom of thought is a good theory, but not when the universe cares only about what you believe is true, rather than what you wish were true, so don't you dare convince people otherwise or billions will die&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A conversation my players always have with non hostile technocrats on the matter. And the poor technocrat is never ready for the answers.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not only will I convince people that man eating dragons exist, but that they have the power to fight the dragons, because not everything is about the negative, and you won't accomplish anything for humanity by pissing your black trousers at the idea of danger&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Shut up you hypocrite, you convinced people of the reality of nuclear warfare and ofthe risks of AI uprising and alien invasions. Don't lecture us on the danger of freedom of thought when you brought more end of the world ideas in the consensus than millenias of mysticism!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And my favorite <br /> &quot;Dude, you're a brainwashed member of an organisation that has gaslighted humanity for nearly five centuries. Your opinion on anything don't matter, firstly because it's probably not your opinion but what you're programmed to believed, second because your organisation lies more than a politician on steroid. I would cast a spell to force you to speak the truth, but I'm afraid you would die immediatly, as truth is your anathema.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T03:02:31-07:00","id":1510870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded?p=1510859#post1510859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if I remember correctly, the book states that technocracts are in a 1984 doublethink state on that matter. Both accepting and denying magic at the the same time</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall anything to that effect. That said, my own head canon on the matter is that the Technocracy features a disproportionate number of agents in Denial: still a small minority, but a <i>loud</i> minority that gives rise to the \u201cthey don't believe in magic\u201d stereotype. (And some of them are so far gone that they instinctively weaponize their Denial and become a kind of Negation Men: the Denial-based Marauder variants that were introduced in <b>Book of Secrets</b>.) So both views <i>exist</i>; just not in the same people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:05:37-07:00","id":1510930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded?p=1510870#post1510870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall anything to that effect. That said, my own head canon on the matter is that the Technocracy features a disproportionate number of agents in Denial: still a small minority, but a <i>loud</i> minority that gives rise to the \u201cthey don't believe in magic\u201d stereotype. (And some of them are so far gone that they instinctively weaponize their Denial and become a kind of Negation Men: the Denial-based Marauder variants that were introduced in <b>Book of Secrets</b>.) So both views <i>exist</i>; just not in the same people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Found it, page 30<br /> Found it, page 30<br /> &quot;As far as the Technocracy is concerned, Union operatives\u200b do not use &quot;magick&quot; and are not &quot;mages&quot; of any kind. This perspective involve a\u200b fair ammount lf cognitive dissonance&quot;<br /> <br /> The text is longer, but I don't know how much I can quote before angering the mods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T19:38:16-07:00","id":1510947,"title":"","content":"As someone who works in Corporate America, the book does a good job of treating things as a HR manual. For me it helped get into the mindset of playing a Technocrat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T02:02:21-07:00","id":1510964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510845-technocracy-reloaded?p=1510930#post1510930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Found it, page 30<br /> Found it, page 30<br /> &quot;As far as the Technocracy is concerned, Union operatives\u200b do not use &quot;magick&quot; and are not &quot;mages&quot; of any kind. This perspective involve a\u200b fair ammount lf cognitive dissonance&quot;<br /> <br /> The text is longer, but I don't know how much I can quote before angering the mods</div> </div> </div> </div>But does it say about what the higher ups believe? Previous books explicitly or implicitly said that the higher ups believe in a lot of things(e.g avatars as spirits) that the grunts don't or the fact that they are mages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T02:12:33-07:00","id":1510966,"title":"","content":"What it says is that Technocrats don't believe that what <i>they</i> do is Magick. That's different from not believing that Magick exists; as I said before, their position is that Magick is real, but that it's wild and dangerous as opposed to the Enlightened Science that <i>they</i> practice. <br /> <br /> The cognitive dissonance isn't about holding 1984-style simultaneous mutually contradictory views on the existence of Magick; it's about rejecting the notion that the Technocracy's Enlightened Science is just another kind of Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}